text She spreads it out on the ground and begins folding it neatly.
text Is she never going to get another chance to wear it?
text Even for just a moment.
text Can we never go back to that time in our lives?
text Will we never get a chance to wrap up all those things we left undone?
text For no particular reason at all... I recall Sunohara's face.
text Sunohara lived in a dorm while in school, but he went back home after graduation.
text I forgot where in the countryside he's from, but I want to say it was the Tohoku region.
text In any case, it's far away.
text Time has driven us apart, and we don't even talk to each other these days.
text He was the only guy I really knew in school...
text That idiot who would mess around in his school uniform...
text But knowing Sunohara, he'd tag along with me no matter what kind of trouble I wanted to get into.
