text An image of Sunohara's good old room flashes before my eyes.
sound NRX.aac
text @[Voice]
text "A company dorm."
text Of course. That place isn't the room I spent all that time in any longer... It's now the room of some other student I've never met.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...In that case, could you tell me how to contact him there?
sound NRY.aac
text @[Voice]
text "Okay... Are you ready?"
text @[Tomoya]
text Yes, please.
text ......
text I hang up the phone, then pick it back up and punch in the number I just jotted down.
sound NRZ.aac
text @[Voice]
text "Yes, this is the Satsuki Dormitory."
text A middle-aged woman's voice.
text @[Tomoya]
text My name is Okazaki, may I speak to a Youhei Sunohara-san?
sound NS0.aac
text @[Voice]
text "Yes, one moment."
text ......
sound NS1.aac
text @[Voice]
text "Hello?"
text I can hear him trying to sound respectable.
text @[Tomoya]
text Sunohara? It's me. It's Okazaki.
sound NS2.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "What...? Okazaki? Seriously?!"
text He instantly switches back to the voice I've always known, as if we'd seen each other just yesterday.
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah. How are you?
sound NS3.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "I'm doing well, but... you won't believe how unfair it is around here. Just listen, I'm sure you'll understand."
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah. I'd be happy to next time, but for now, listen.
sound NS4.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Tch, so you're still the boss of me even after we graduated?"
text @[Tomoya]
text Just like the old days, right?
sound NS5.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "So, what is it?"
text @[Tomoya]
text I want to hold a graduation ceremony.
sound NS6.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Huh...?"
text @[Tomoya]
text You know how Nagisa graduated this spring, right?
sound NS7.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Oh, Nagisa-chan. So you two are still going out? That's impressive."
text @[Tomoya]
text Forget about that part, stupid. Just listen.
text We start to slip back into our groove, trading insults back and forth.
text @[Tomoya]
text This past year, she's been pushing herself to go to school every day, even though she's all alone there with no friends.
text @[Tomoya]
text But in the end, she wasn't able to go to graduation.
text @[Tomoya]
text Isn't that sad?
text @[Tomoya]
text So I want to have a graduation ceremony with the old gang.
text @[Tomoya]
text It was only for a month, but we were closer to her than anyone else back then.
sound NS8.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "..."
text @[Tomoya]
text Please, Sunohara.
sound NS9.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "..."
sound NSA.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "I'm in the middle of training right now..."
sound NSB.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "I'd be fired if I went to do something like that..."
text @[Tomoya]
text Sorry to hear that.
sound NSC.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "So you want me to get fired?!"
text @[Tomoya]
text You won't get fired just because you miss one day.
sound NSD.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Yes, I will."
text @[Tomoya]
text Not very flexible, are you?
sound NSE.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "It's not me who isn't 'flexible,' it's my company."
text @[Tomoya]
text Are you sure you can't make it happen?
sound NSF.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Well, if my days off line up..."
sound NSG.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "But I'd still have to go and come back within a day, right...? That'd be tough."
text @[Tomoya]
text C'mon, do it for my sake.
sound NSH.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Don't you mean for Nagisa-chan's sake?"
text @[Tomoya]
text Same thing.
sound NSI.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Then I'll try to take just one day off. I don't know when it's going to be, though."
text @[Tomoya]
text Don't worry, I'll work around it.
sound NSJ.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Then I'll contact you next time."
text @[Tomoya]
text Er, could you not call?
sound NSK.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Why not?"
text @[Tomoya]
text Because Nagisa might pick up the phone.
sound NSL.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "..."
text @[Tomoya]
text She'd figure out what we're up to if she did, right?
sound NSM.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "..."
text @[Tomoya]
text Hello?
sound NSN.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Are you..."
sound NSO.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "...living together with Nagisa-chan...?"
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah, did I not tell you?
sound NSP.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "It's been a full year since we last talked."
text @[Tomoya]
text Oh, sorry. I just haven't had the time.
sound NSQ.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "You sure do seem to be living a happy life!"
text @[Tomoya]
text Geez, sorry.
sound NSR.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "I'm feeling less and less inclined to put my job on the line just to go out there and meet you."
text @[Tomoya]
text Show up even if you don't feel inclined.
sound NSS.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "What a great guy I am!"
text @[Tomoya]
text That's why I'm asking you.
sound NST.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "..."
sound NSU.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Tch... Fine."
sound NSV.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "Call me back around this hour. You should be able to reach me."
text @[Tomoya]
text Okay, I will.
sound NSW.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text "See ya."
text @[Tomoya]
text Yo.
text I put the receiver down.
text It felt like I was back acting stupid with him again.
text I feel like I could really make this graduation ceremony happen, or anything else, for that matter.
text Yeah.
text We were able to beat the basketball team with that rag-tag group and reform the shell of the drama club into a unit that performed at the Founder's Festival.
text If we can just act like we did then, nothing is impossible.
